  "assumptions": [
    "One voxel is one Minecraft block. Slab and stair geometry is encoded in block states, not half-scale coordinates. No perspective rescaling of printed measurements.",
    "Images were inspected in the supplied order. The main photograph is the appearance reference; numbered construction diagrams constrain the geometry. Partial construction/cutaway renders are not additional builds.",
    "Photographs do not uniquely determine every voxel. All geometry outside explicitly printed dimensions is an interpretation, not an assertion of exact recovery. Numeric coordinates below specify the actual choices.",
    "No player, animal, surrounding landscape, grass, clouds, loose scenic hay outside the illustrated building, fluids, entities, chest inventories or complex block-entity payloads are included.",
    "No live-server test: local NBT/registry/reader verification cannot prove survival placement order, neighbor-update stability or exact photographic fidelity.",
    "Printed 12x17 interpreted as the outer dirt/wall rectangle, not including eaves or side pen. Both gable ends reconstructed symmetrically from opposite-corner construction views.",
    "Gable silhouette chosen as courses x2..11 at y8,x3..10 at y9,x4..9 at y10,x6..7 at y11. Roof covers/extends parts of this silhouette. Width-even central 2-cell ridge preserves the printed 12-cell wall.",
    "Curved roof profile is enumerated in dimension_audit. Exact half-step transition cannot be counted unequivocally in the photograph. Two central bottom slabs at y12; straight birch stairs face uphill east/west. Slab types as explicitly recorded. One-block front/rear/side eaves inferred. No extra hidden roof filling except gable gap closure.",
    "Doors inferred 4 wide by4 high at x5..8, both ends. White jambs x4,9 and header x3..10,y5. Loft frames x5..8,y7..10 with2x2 pane cores. The visible four window quadrants are interpreted as a2x2 block opening, not four panes in one block.",
    "Long-wall windows are two2x2 pane openings z4..5 and12..13,y2..3 per side, with white vertical shutters atz3,6,11,14. Undepicted long wall mirrored. No horizontal white sill is invented.",
    "Red concrete is the primary wall, terracotta forms panels, and sparse supported low powder courses represent the mottled red finish. Exact patch locations are inferred; powder y1..2 is placed over dirt/solid wall to avoid unsupported powder.",
    "Side pen is x13..17,z7..11 with fence enclosure, inferred central east gate, front corner fence supports throughy4 and stepped birch slab canopy x12..17,z6..12. The gate location/state is not legible; chosen closed,facingeast. Canopy and pen footprint are lower-confidence inferred dimensions.",
    "Eight birch crossbeams spanx2..11 at y7,z2,4,...16; spacing inferred from step5. The ceiling is otherwise open, not a solid invented loft floor.",
    "Interior reconstructed from cutaway step8: four fence partitions atz3,7,11,15,x9..11; inner posts extend toy3. Ten specified hay stacks at west rear/front corners and east stalls; exact quantities/positions not printed. Four wall torches atx2/11,y4,z6/12 face into room. No troughs/chests/mobs added.",
    "Ventilator locationx5..7,z11..13 and heighty12..16 inferred from step7. Hollow3x3 red ring with open central shaft, four birch fence corner supports aty14, notched5x5 stair/plank cap aty15 and3x3 bottom-slab crown aty16. No smoke, campfire or chimney block entities.",
    "Fence and pane connection states are explicitly generated from adjacent solid/fence/pane cells. Stair shapes straight; no corner roof stairs beyond the notched vent cap are inferred. Hidden neighbor update behavior remains untested."
  ],
